From 057b3f2c2737e13156aee110cf21c81f887c1c22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vijay Anand Raghava Kanakagiri <svskvar@amazon.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 21:17:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/24] [Distributed] Make DDP tests accelerator-agnostic
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace hard-coded CUDA/NCCL references in DDP test infrastructure and
test files with accelerator-generic equivalents, enabling these tests to
run on any backend registered via PrivateUse1 or the accelerator API.

**Source changes (torch/testing/_internal/common_distributed.py):**
- `skip_if_lt_x_gpu`: Use `torch.accelerator.is_available()` and
  `torch.accelerator.device_count()` instead of per-backend checks
  (cuda/hpu/xpu).
- `requires_accelerator_dist_backend`: Detect PrivateUse1 backends
  via `Backend.default_device_backend_map`.
- `DistributedTestBase.backend()`: Look up backend from
  `Backend.default_device_backend_map` instead of hardcoding
  device→backend mapping.
- `DistributedTestBase.create_pg()`: Use `ACCELERATOR_DIST_BACKENDS`
  set instead of checking for specific backend names.
- `MultiProcContinuousTest`: Handle `classmethod` and `property`
  descriptors for `device_type` attribute resolution.

**Test changes:**
- Rename `gpus_for_rank` → `devices_for_rank` across all DDP test files.
- In `test_c10d_nccl.py`: introduce `DEVICE_TYPE` and `BACKEND`
  module-level constants derived from `torch.accelerator`; replace
  `@requires_nccl()` with `@requires_accelerator_dist_backend()`;
  replace hardcoded `"cuda"` and `"nccl"` strings; rename test methods
  to remove `_nccl` suffix; guard CUDA-only code paths
  (NCCL env vars, nccl version checks) behind `DEVICE_TYPE == "cuda"`.
- In `test_c10d_gloo.py`, `test_c10d_ucc.py`, `test_ddp_hooks.py`:
  update `gpus_for_rank` → `devices_for_rank` import.
- Add `test_ddp_buffer_sync_multi_forward_with_batchnorm` test.

CUDA remains fully supported — it becomes one of many possible backends
rather than the only assumed one.
